02:23:16.300 --> 02:23:17.920
get going. I just want to get away from them.

02:23:18.440 --> 02:23:20.120
There's old Gordon Spector chomping at a bit

02:23:20.120 --> 02:23:22.240
complaining. I had to get away from them, you know.

02:23:22.610 --> 02:23:24.250
Whole car run good, and I'm really happy

02:23:24.250 --> 02:23:26.190
the way everything went for everybody. I'd like to thank all the

02:23:26.190 --> 02:23:27.580
sponsors. I'd like to

02:23:27.580 --> 02:23:30.000
send our condolences to two

02:23:30.000 --> 02:23:32.300
T. Wayne who lost his father.

02:23:32.300 --> 02:23:34.440
And I like to take all those Democrats

02:23:34.440 --> 02:23:36.280
and that are trying to get a tobacco out here

02:23:36.280 --> 02:23:37.440
and tell them to stick it up you know where.

02:23:37.440 --> 02:23:39.430
Vote Dole, man, do that.

02:23:39.430 --> 02:23:41.970
- Hey, speaking of which, talking about victories,

02:23:41.970 --> 02:23:45.270
your win tonight gives Ford the manufacturer's point lead.

02:23:45.270 --> 02:23:46.090
- Well, that's good.

02:23:46.090 --> 02:23:48.610
At least I can add to something and I love it.

02:23:48.610 --> 02:23:50.280
I just like to thank my entire team,

02:23:50.280 --> 02:23:51.620
the engine department, everybody,

02:23:51.620 --> 02:23:54.460
all our sponsors, Fleetwood, Mobile,

02:23:54.460 --> 02:23:56.920
Mead Paper Company, Miller Brewing Company, Goodyear.

02:23:56.920 --> 02:23:58.120
The tires were really great today.

02:23:58.120 --> 02:24:00.000
You know, we didn't like the tires first race.

02:24:00.000 --> 02:24:01.660
These were really awful good tires.

02:24:02.080 --> 02:24:04.920
Hey, your engine builder, Mike Eggie, told you you would not have a problem again

02:24:04.920 --> 02:24:08.260
like you had last week at Michigan, losing the motor, and he kept his promise.

02:24:08.380 --> 02:24:10.140
Yeah, that deal last week was an awful fluke,

02:24:10.180 --> 02:24:12.340
and it's one thing when you lose a motor and you don't know why,

02:24:12.400 --> 02:24:14.680
but we know exactly why the motor went, and that's good.

02:24:14.720 --> 02:24:16.800
We haven't had any engine problems to speak of all year long,

02:24:16.900 --> 02:24:18.120
and the car's been fast.

02:24:18.200 --> 02:24:19.420
You know, I screwed up a Watkins Glen.

02:24:19.500 --> 02:24:20.540
We lost a motor at Michigan.

02:24:20.920 --> 02:24:22.740
This is our fifth win, and we're still going for 10.

02:24:23.300 --> 02:24:26.500
Rusty Wallace in victory lane for the fifth time in 1996.

02:24:26.750 --> 02:24:27.510
Hey, what a celebration.

02:24:27.630 --> 02:24:29.850
Let's check in with the second-place finisher, Jeff Gordon.

02:24:29.870 --> 02:24:30.000
Oh, my God.

02:24:30.800 --> 02:24:34.080
well jeff you had a heck of a run but you needed longer green flag

02:24:34.080 --> 02:24:37.440
runs i tell you what i've never felt better after a bristol race i'm ready to

02:24:37.440 --> 02:24:39.840
go another hundred laps we can arrange that

02:24:39.840 --> 02:24:43.760
i wish i could have you know my car was so strong on long runs it just

02:24:43.760 --> 02:24:46.810
took it forever to get going but man once i got my rhythm

02:24:46.810 --> 02:24:50.330
once the tires you know came to our pressures man that thing was strong

02:24:50.330 --> 02:24:53.770
we showed that early on but you know rusty was so strong i just have to let

02:24:53.770 --> 02:24:58.010
him go because he was eating us up on new tires and on short runs but

02:24:58.010 --> 02:25:00.000
i really believe you know that we could have run

02:25:00.060 --> 02:25:01.880
and run them down. We were running them down there at the end.

02:25:02.220 --> 02:25:03.920
I'll tell you, lap cars were just off,

02:25:04.000 --> 02:25:06.020
which is normal here for Bristol, and you

02:25:06.020 --> 02:25:07.900
got to deal with that, but I'm real happy

02:25:07.900 --> 02:25:10.020
with a second-place finish. Just a strong

02:25:10.020 --> 02:25:11.600
effort. This is what we need to do tonight.

02:25:11.880 --> 02:25:14.020
And you picked up a few points, sole possession of second

02:25:14.020 --> 02:25:16.070
place now. Well, you know, you always

02:25:16.070 --> 02:25:18.170
won't win. I mean, I can't ever forget

02:25:18.170 --> 02:25:19.970
about that, but, you know, the points

02:25:19.970 --> 02:25:22.210
are definitely there. We still got, you

02:25:22.210 --> 02:25:23.870
know, nine or ten races left to go, and

02:25:23.870 --> 02:25:25.870
we gained on them. That's what we got to do, and

02:25:25.870 --> 02:25:28.210
I'm real proud of the team. They kept me up front,

02:25:28.330 --> 02:25:30.000
and track positions are real important here, so

02:25:30.030 --> 02:25:34.010
So I want to, you know, thank God for keeping everything safe on that car, man.

02:25:34.070 --> 02:25:37.490
I tell you, all four fenders are on it, and that's saying something when you leave here.

02:25:37.690 --> 02:25:38.970
And he came home second tonight.

02:25:39.440 --> 02:25:45.580
There you've heard from the first two finishers, Rusty Wallace the winner and Jeff Gordon second place.

02:25:45.580 --> 02:25:51.710
And as we indicated, Ford now has possession of the Manufacturers Championship.

02:25:51.870 --> 02:25:55.310
Jeff Gordon in sole possession of second place in the point standings.

02:25:55.390 --> 02:25:56.110
Back in a moment.
